### Component 1: MongoDB Lead Model

#### [NEW] [Lead.ts](file:///c:/Users/DES%2002/Documents/Aditya/FMCG/fmcg-next-vercel/src/models/Lead.ts)

A Mongoose model following the exact pattern used in [Brand.ts](file:///c:/Users/DES%2002/Documents/Aditya/FMCG/fmcg-next-vercel/src/models/Brand.ts) (`models.X || model<I>('X', Schema)`).

**Purpose:** Persist every lead inquiry regardless of WhatsApp API success/failure. Ensures zero lead loss.

```typescript
import mongoose, { Schema, model, models } from 'mongoose';

export interface ILead {
  _id?: string;
  name: string;
  phone: string;
  message: string;
  source: 'whatsapp_widget';
  whatsappStatus: 'pending' | 'sent' | 'template_sent' | 'delivered' | 'read' | 'failed';
  whatsappMessageId?: string;
  whatsappError?: string;
  createdAt?: Date;
  updatedAt?: Date;
}

const LeadSchema = new Schema<ILead>(
  {
    name:              { type: String, required: true },
    phone:             { type: String, required: true },
    message:           { type: String, required: true },
    source:            { type: String, default: 'whatsapp_widget' },
    whatsappStatus:    { type: String, enum: ['pending','sent','template_sent','delivered','read','failed'], default: 'pending' },
    whatsappMessageId: { type: String, default: '' },
    whatsappError:     { type: String, default: '' },
  },
  { timestamps: true }
);

const Lead = models.Lead || model<ILead>('Lead', LeadSchema);
export default Lead;
```

**Fields explained:**

| Field | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| `name` | Visitor's name from widget lead form |
| `phone` | Visitor's phone from widget lead form |
| `message` | The inquiry text |
| `source` | Always `'whatsapp_widget'` — future-proofs for other lead sources |
| `whatsappStatus` | Tracks lifecycle: `pending` → `sent`/`template_sent` → `delivered` → `read` / `failed` |
| `whatsappMessageId` | Meta's message ID (e.g., `wamid.xxx`) — used by webhook to update status |
| `whatsappError` | Stores error message if API call fails — for debugging |

